tasks.context:
Create scripts/scs001/hook-formula-tracker.ts — tracks which of the 9 hook formulas perform best.

The script should:
1. Read workspace/scs001/batch-output.json to get the generated hooks with formula tags
2. Accept manual metric input via --add-metrics flag: --video-id, --formula, --retention-3s (0-100), --completion-rate (0-100), --comment-rate (float)
3. Store metrics in workspace/scs001/hook-formula-metrics.json:
   {
     formulas: {
       'curiosity_gap': { count: number, avg_retention_3s: number, avg_completion: number, avg_comment_rate: number },
       'contrarian': { ... },
       // ... all 9 formulas
     },
     last_updated: string
   }
4. With --report flag, print a ranked table of formulas by avg_retention_3s descending
5. With --recommend flag, output the top 3 formulas to weight more heavily in next batch generation

This feeds SCS001 Part 12's iteration loop: batch volume generates performance data, performance data sharpens the next batch.
